# Third-Party Source Register

Generated by {{skill_name}} v{{skill_version}}.

Use this register in proportion to intended actions. Ordinary citations remain in `sources/`; add entries here for external code, data, models, or other reusable material that is inspected, executed, incorporated, or redistributed.

## Source Entry Template

- Name and owner: [record]
- Stable identity: [URL, version, commit, DOI, or dataset release]
- Intended use: [inspect, execute, incorporate, or redistribute]
- Inspected or used surface: [record]
- Dependencies or excluded payloads: [record when material]
- Licence or terms evidence: [required when intended action makes it material]
- Provenance notes: [record when material]
- Limitations and unresolved questions: [record]
- Integration decision: [not applicable, permitted, deferred, or blocked with reason]

## Proportionality

- Local inspection or execution requires identity, scope, and limitations.
- A research checkout may use any host-approved location and should remain uncommitted when it is not being incorporated; an outside-repository location is not a universal requirement.
- Copying, adapting, committing, packaging, or redistributing requires stronger licence and provenance evidence.
- An unresolved Level 3 integration question does not automatically block Level 1 citation or ordinary source review.
